From 3a0f4434400f13b12fb354a3513a3c9c9eab9949 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:42:13 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Cheats: PPSSPP's CWCheat files, and a port's own on the menu

A player's PPSSPP cheat file, PSP/Cheats/<disc id>.ini on the memory stick,
is read and run as PPSSPP runs it: every cheat that is on, from its first
line, every 77 ms of the game's time, from a vblank hook. Every CWCheat code
type is run with PPSSPP's meaning (host/cheats/cwcheat.cpp: writes, serial
writes, copies, pointer codes with their extra lines, boolean ops, the
conditions and the button joker); Action Replay lines are read and not run.
A write into recompiled code (the executable's code sections, or an
overlay's header and code: overlay_code_overlaps) is left out, and the
menu says the cheat changes code.

GameProfile::cheats lists a port's own: a key, a heading, a name, a sentence
and choices, each a label and CWCheat lines. They run through the same
engine, before the file's, and are saved in settings.ini's cheats.builtin
("key=choice,..."; <prefix>_CHEATS sets it for a run).

The menu has a Cheats page, before System: Use cheats (cheats.enabled), the
port's own under their headings, and a PPSSPP cheat file row that opens a
page of the file's cheats, which turns them on and off and writes the file
back. <prefix>_NO_CHEATS=1 turns all of it off; <prefix>_TRACE_CHEATS=1
logs each pass; <prefix>_CHEAT_INTERVAL_MS sets another interval.

Tested on Windows with Dissidia 012 (USA): tests/cwcheat_tests.cpp (30
checks of the parser and every code type); a file's code at a heap address
gave the same result as in PPSSPP 1.20.4, whose memory layout was compared
at the same screen; the port's own money, item and battle cheats on the
game's screens; the page, the file page, and saving from the pad. Not
tested: a Linux build, Android, a code that writes into code, the button
joker from a real pad.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
