 `glyph_cache` is for changing the font while a game runs. A game that caches the glyphs it has drawn keeps them until its atlas needs the cell, so a new font shows only in text it has not drawn yet. Where the game keeps that atlas, read off its own text code, lets the framework make it draw them again. Null for any game nobody has traced.
 
+`cheats` lists cheats the port offers on the menu's Cheats page, beside the player's own PPSSPP cheat file (`PSP/Cheats/<disc id>.ini` on the memory stick, `host/cheats/cheats.hpp`). Each is a `BuiltinCheat`: a key for settings.ini, the heading it goes under, a name, a sentence for the footer, and its choices, each a label and its CWCheat code lines (what a cheat file has after `_L`). One choice makes a switch; several make Off and each. They run through the same engine as the file, before it, every 77 ms of the game's time, so a code written as a player would write it gives the same result. A write into recompiled code is left out, as for the file; such a code needs the interpreter, which cheats do not reach yet. Test each against the game's own screens before listing it: a public list's codes can name an address the game no longer reads. Without any, the page has only the switch and the file.
+
 `interpolation_thresholds` is for frame interpolation, which blends the game's frames and must not blend across a camera cut. The angles and fractions it uses to tell a cut from motion hold for any game; its distances are in the game's own world units, and the defaults were measured on Monster Hunter Portable 3rd. A game whose world is on a very different scale gives its own; one that does not, gets those defaults.
 
 A driver writes into the game's memory, so check the code it relies on before it writes anything — Yakumo compares every instruction and constant it depends on at start-up, from `patch_loaded_image`, and stays out, saying why, if one differs.
diff --git a/host/cheats/cheats.cpp b/host/cheats/cheats.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9e4931f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/cheats/cheats.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,286 @@
+#include "cheats/cheats.hpp"
+
+#include "cheats/cwcheat.hpp"
+#include "hle/hle_common.hpp"
+#include "kernel/kernel.hpp"
+#include "overlays.hpp"
+#include "profile.hpp"
+#include "settings/settings.hpp"
+
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <fstream>
+#include <iostream>
+#include <mutex>
+#include <span>
+#include <sstream>
+#include <utility>
+
+namespace portablekit::cheats {
+namespace {
+
+constexpr std::uint64_t kDefaultIntervalUs = 77'000u;  // PPSSPP's default refresh
+
+struct State {
+    std::mutex lock;
+    psprecomp::Runtime *runtime{};
+    std::vector<std::pair<std::uint32_t, std::uint32_t>> code;  // the executable's code, [start, end)
+    std::filesystem::path memory_stick;
+    std::filesystem::path path;
+    bool loaded{};
+    bool file_found{};
+    std::string problem;
+    CheatFile file;
+    std::vector<bool> changes_code;
+    // The port's own: each one's choices, and the one that is on (0: none).
+    std::vector<std::vector<Cheat>> builtin;
+    std::vector<std::size_t> builtin_choice;
+    std::vector<bool> builtin_changes_code;
+    std::uint64_t interval_us{kDefaultIntervalUs};
+    std::uint64_t next_us{};
+};
+
+State &state() {
+    static State s;
+    return s;
+}
+
+bool trace() {
+    static const bool on = env("TRACE_CHEATS") != nullptr;
+    return on;
+}
+
+// The game's memory as cheats see it.
+class GameMemory final : public Memory {
+public:
+    GameMemory(psprecomp::GuestMemory &memory, const State &s) : memory_(memory), state_(s) {}
+
+    bool valid(std::uint32_t address, std::uint32_t size) const override {
+        return size != 0u && memory_.raw_pointer(address, size) != nullptr;
+    }
+    std::uint8_t read8(std::uint32_t address) const override { return memory_.load8(address); }
+    void write8(std::uint32_t address, std::uint8_t value) override { memory_.store8(address, value); }
+    bool code(std::uint32_t address, std::uint32_t size) const override {
+        const std::uint64_t end = static_cast<std::uint64_t>(address) + size;
+        for (const auto &[from, to] : state_.code)
+            if (address < to && from < end) return true;
+        return overlay_code_overlaps(memory_, address, size);
+    }
+
+private:
+    psprecomp::GuestMemory &memory_;
+    const State &state_;
+};
+
+// One choice of a built-in cheat, read as a file's cheat would be.
+Cheat builtin_cheat(const BuiltinCheat &cheat, const CheatChoice &choice) {
+    std::string text = std::string("_C1 ") + cheat.name + "\n";
+    std::istringstream lines(choice.code != nullptr ? choice.code : "");
+    for (std::string line; std::getline(lines, line);)
+        if (line.find_first_not_of(" \t\r") != std::string::npos) text += "_L " + line + "\n";
+    CheatFile file = parse(text, game().disc_id);
+    if (file.problems != 0u || file.cheats.size() != 1u)
+        std::cerr << "[cheats] the built-in cheat \"" << cheat.name << "\" has lines that cannot be read\n";
+    return file.cheats.empty() ? Cheat{} : std::move(file.cheats.front());
+}
+
+// The built-in cheats that are on, from settings.ini's "key=choice,...".
+// Called with the lock held.
+void read_builtin_choices(State &s) {
+    const std::span<const BuiltinCheat> cheats = game().cheats;
+    s.builtin_choice.assign(cheats.size(), 0u);
+    std::istringstream entries(settings::current().builtin_cheats);
+    for (std::string entry; std::getline(entries, entry, ',');) {
+        const std::size_t equals = entry.find('=');
+        const std::string key = entry.substr(0, equals);
+        const std::size_t choice =
+            equals == std::string::npos ? 1u : static_cast<std::size_t>(std::atoi(entry.c_str() + equals + 1));
+        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < cheats.size(); ++i)
+            if (key == cheats[i].key && choice <= cheats[i].choices.size()) s.builtin_choice[i] = choice;
+    }
+}
+
+void write_builtin_choices(const State &s) {
+    const std::span<const BuiltinCheat> cheats = game().cheats;
+    std::string text;
+    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < cheats.size(); ++i) {
+        if (s.builtin_choice[i] == 0u) continue;
+        if (!text.empty()) text += ",";
+        text += std::string(cheats[i].key) + "=" + std::to_string(s.builtin_choice[i]);
+    }
+    settings::current().builtin_cheats = text;
+    settings::save();
+}
+
+// Reads the file for the disc running now. Called with the lock held.
+void load(State &s) {
+    s.loaded = true;
+    s.file = CheatFile{};
+    s.changes_code.clear();
+    s.problem.clear();
+    const std::string disc_id = active_disc_id();
+    const std::filesystem::path folder = s.memory_stick / "PSP" / "Cheats";
+    s.path = folder / (disc_id + ".ini");
+    // The folder is made so that a player can see where the file goes.
+    std::error_code ec;
+    std::filesystem::create_directories(folder, ec);
+    std::ifstream in(s.path, std::ios::binary);
+    s.file_found = static_cast<bool>(in);
+    if (!s.file_found) {
+        std::cout << "[cheats] no cheat file (" << s.path.string() << ")\n";
+        return;
+    }
+    std::ostringstream text;
+    text << in.rdbuf();
+    s.file = parse(text.str(), disc_id);
+    s.changes_code.assign(s.file.cheats.size(), false);
+    std::size_t on = 0u;
+    for (const Cheat &cheat : s.file.cheats) on += cheat.enabled ? 1u : 0u;
+    std::cout << "[cheats] " << s.file.cheats.size() << " cheats for " << disc_id << " in " << s.path.string() << ", "
+              << on << " on";
+    if (s.file.problems != 0u) std::cout << "; " << s.file.problems << " lines could not be read";
+    std::cout << "\n";
+}
+
+// Writes the file back, as a whole, through a temporary file.
+void save(State &s) {
+    const std::filesystem::path temporary = s.path.string() + ".tmp";
+    {
+        std::ofstream out(temporary, std::ios::binary | std::ios::trunc);
+        out << text_of(s.file);
+        if (!out) {
+            s.problem = "The cheat file could not be saved.";
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+    std::error_code ec;
+    std::filesystem::rename(temporary, s.path, ec);
+    if (ec) {
+        std::filesystem::remove(temporary, ec);
+        s.problem = "The cheat file could not be saved.";
+    }
+}
+
+// Each vblank: a pass when the interval has passed on the game's clock.
+void on_vblank() {
+    State &s = state();
+    const std::uint64_t now = kernel().now_us();
+    if (now < s.next_us) return;
+    s.next_us = now + s.interval_us;
+    if (!settings::current().cheats) return;
+    const std::lock_guard<std::mutex> hold(s.lock);
+    if (!s.loaded) load(s);
+    if (s.runtime == nullptr) return;
+    const std::uint32_t buttons = first_pad_sample_now().buttons;
+    GameMemory memory(s.runtime->memory(), s);
+    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < s.builtin.size(); ++i) {
+        if (s.builtin_choice[i] == 0u) continue;
+        const Cheat &cheat = s.builtin[i][s.builtin_choice[i] - 1u];
+        const RunResult result = run(cheat, memory, buttons);
+        if (result.wrote_code && !s.builtin_changes_code[i]) {
+            s.builtin_changes_code[i] = true;
+            std::cout << "[cheats] \"" << cheat.name
+                      << "\" writes into the game's code, which is not supported yet; its other writes are made\n";
+        }
+        if (trace()) std::cout << "[cheats] ran the built-in \"" << cheat.name << "\"\n";
+    }
+    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < s.file.cheats.size(); ++i) {
+        const Cheat &cheat = s.file.cheats[i];
+        if (!cheat.enabled) continue;
+        const RunResult result = run(cheat, memory, buttons);
+        if (result.wrote_code && !s.changes_code[i]) {
+            s.changes_code[i] = true;
+            std::cout << "[cheats] \"" << cheat.name
+                      << "\" writes into the game's code, which is not supported yet; its other writes are made\n";
+        }
+        if (trace())
+            std::cout << "[cheats] ran \"" << cheat.name << "\"" << (result.wrote_code ? ", code write left out" : "")
+                      << (result.invalid ? ", stopped at a line it cannot run" : "") << "\n";
+    }
+}
+
+} // namespace
+
+void install(psprecomp::Runtime &runtime, const psprecomp::Elf32Image &elf, const std::filesystem::path &memory_stick) {
+    if (env("NO_CHEATS") != nullptr) {
+        std::cout << "[cheats] " << env_name("NO_CHEATS") << ": no cheats\n";
+        return;
+    }
+    State &s = state();
+    s.runtime = &runtime;
+    s.memory_stick = memory_stick;
+    for (const BuiltinCheat &cheat : game().cheats) {
+        std::vector<Cheat> choices;
+        for (const CheatChoice &choice : cheat.choices) choices.push_back(builtin_cheat(cheat, choice));
+        s.builtin.push_back(std::move(choices));
+    }
+    s.builtin_changes_code.assign(s.builtin.size(), false);
+    read_builtin_choices(s);
+    // The executable's code: its code sections, or else its executable
+    // segments.
+    constexpr std::uint32_t kExecutableSection = 0x4u, kExecutableSegment = 0x1u;
+    for (const psprecomp::ElfSection &section : elf.sections())
+        if ((section.flags & kExecutableSection) != 0u && section.size != 0u) {
+            const std::uint32_t start = elf.section_runtime_address(section, game().load_base);
+            s.code.emplace_back(start, start + section.size);
+        }
+    if (s.code.empty())
+        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < elf.segments().size(); ++i)
+            if (const psprecomp::ElfSegment &segment = elf.segments()[i];
+                segment.type == 1u && (segment.flags & kExecutableSegment) != 0u) {
+                const std::uint32_t start = elf.segment_runtime_address(i, game().load_base);
+                s.code.emplace_back(start, start + segment.memory_size);
+            }
+    if (const char *ms = env("CHEAT_INTERVAL_MS"); ms != nullptr && std::atoi(ms) > 0)
+        s.interval_us = static_cast<std::uint64_t>(std::atoi(ms)) * 1000u;
+    kernel().add_vblank_hook(on_vblank);
+}
+
+Overview overview() {
+    State &s = state();
+    const std::lock_guard<std::mutex> hold(s.lock);
+    Overview o;
+    o.available = s.runtime != nullptr;
+    if (!o.available) return o;
+    if (!s.loaded) load(s);
+    o.file = s.path;
+    o.file_found = s.file_found;
+    o.problem = s.problem;
+    o.unreadable_lines = s.file.problems;
+    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < s.file.cheats.size(); ++i) {
+        const Cheat &cheat = s.file.cheats[i];
+        o.cheats.push_back({cheat.name, cheat.enabled, s.changes_code[i], cheat.action_replay});
+    }
+    const std::span<const BuiltinCheat> cheats = game().cheats;
+    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < s.builtin.size(); ++i) {
+        BuiltinRow row{cheats[i].section, cheats[i].name, cheats[i].description ? cheats[i].description : "", {},
+                       s.builtin_choice[i], s.builtin_changes_code[i]};
+        if (cheats[i].choices.size() > 1u)
+            for (const CheatChoice &choice : cheats[i].choices) row.labels.emplace_back(choice.label);
+        o.builtin.push_back(std::move(row));
+    }
+    return o;
+}
+
+void set_enabled(std::size_t index, bool enabled) {
+    State &s = state();
+    const std::lock_guard<std::mutex> hold(s.lock);
+    if (index >= s.file.cheats.size()) return;
+    cheats::set_enabled(s.file, index, enabled);
+    save(s);
+}
+
+void set_builtin(std::size_t index, std::size_t choice) {
+    State &s = state();
+    const std::lock_guard<std::mutex> hold(s.lock);
+    if (index >= s.builtin.size() || choice > s.builtin[index].size()) return;
+    s.builtin_choice[index] = choice;
+    write_builtin_choices(s);
+}
+
+void reload() {
+    State &s = state();
+    const std::lock_guard<std::mutex> hold(s.lock);
+    if (s.runtime != nullptr) load(s);
+}
+
+} // namespace portablekit::cheats
diff --git a/host/cheats/cheats.hpp b/host/cheats/cheats.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c7cdf37
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/cheats/cheats.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+#pragma once
+
+// Cheats: the port's own (GameProfile::cheats, on or off in settings.ini's
+// cheats.builtin) and the player's CWCheat file, PSP/Cheats/<DISCID>.ini on
+// the memory stick as PPSSPP keeps it (cwcheat.hpp), read when the game
+// starts. Both run as PPSSPP runs a file: every cheat that is on, from its
+// first line, every 77 ms of the game's time, on the game's own clock (a
+// vblank hook); the port's own first. The menu's Cheats page turns them on and
+// off, and writes the file's back to the file.
+//
+// Recompiled code does not change when memory does, so a write into the
+// game's code (its executable's code sections, or an overlay's header and
+// code, overlays.hpp) is left out and the page says the cheat changes code.
+// <prefix>_CHEATS="key=choice,...": the port's own that are on, as
+// settings.ini's cheats.builtin. <prefix>_NO_CHEATS=1: no cheats at all. <prefix>_CHEAT_INTERVAL_MS: another
+// interval. <prefix>_TRACE_CHEATS=1: each pass's cheats, with what they did.
+
+#include "psprecomp/elf32.hpp"
+#include "psprecomp/runtime.hpp"
+
+#include <cstddef>
+#include <filesystem>
+#include <string>
+#include <vector>
+
+namespace portablekit::cheats {
+
+// From install_system, once the kernel is installed.
+void install(psprecomp::Runtime &runtime, const psprecomp::Elf32Image &elf, const std::filesystem::path &memory_stick);
+
+// What the menu shows.
+struct CheatRow {
+    std::string name;
+    bool enabled{};
+    bool changes_code{};   // a write of it into code was left out
+    bool action_replay{};  // its codes are Action Replay ones: not run
+};
+
+// One of the port's own cheats.
+struct BuiltinRow {
+    std::string section;
+    std::string name;
+    std::string description;
+    std::vector<std::string> labels;  // its choices; empty: it is a switch
+    std::size_t choice{};             // 0: off; otherwise the choice's number, from 1
+    bool changes_code{};
+};
+
+struct Overview {
+    bool available{};  // installed, and not turned off by the variable
+    std::filesystem::path file;
+    bool file_found{};
+    std::string problem;  // why the file could not be read or saved, if it could not
+    std::size_t unreadable_lines{};
+    std::vector<CheatRow> cheats;
+    std::vector<BuiltinRow> builtin;
+};
+
+[[nodiscard]] Overview overview();
+// Turns a cheat on or off and saves the file.
+void set_enabled(std::size_t index, bool enabled);
+// Sets one of the port's own: 0 off, or a choice's number from 1. Saved in
+// settings.ini.
+void set_builtin(std::size_t index, std::size_t choice);
+// Reads the file again (after the player has changed it).
+void reload();
+
+} // namespace portablekit::cheats
diff --git a/host/cheats/cwcheat.cpp b/host/cheats/cwcheat.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c733ae8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/cheats/cwcheat.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,443 @@
+#include "cheats/cwcheat.hpp"
+
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <cctype>
+#include <optional>
+
+namespace portablekit::cheats {
+namespace {
+
+// --- Reading the file --------------------------------------------------------
+
+std::string_view trim(std::string_view s) {
+    while (!s.empty() && std::isspace(static_cast<unsigned char>(s.front()))) s.remove_prefix(1);
+    while (!s.empty() && std::isspace(static_cast<unsigned char>(s.back()))) s.remove_suffix(1);
+    return s;
+}
+
+// A disc id as it compares: no dashes, upper case.
+std::string id_key(std::string_view id) {
+    std::string key;
+    for (const char c : id)
+        if (c != '-' && !std::isspace(static_cast<unsigned char>(c)))
+            key.push_back(static_cast<char>(std::toupper(static_cast<unsigned char>(c))));
+    return key;
+}
+
+// A hex word, "0x" optional; the rest of `s` after it.
+std::optional<std::uint32_t> hex_word(std::string_view &s) {
+    s = trim(s);
+    if (s.size() >= 2u && s[0] == '0' && (s[1] == 'x' || s[1] == 'X')) s.remove_prefix(2);
+    std::uint32_t value = 0u;
+    std::size_t digits = 0u;
+    while (digits < s.size() && std::isxdigit(static_cast<unsigned char>(s[digits]))) {
+        const char c = static_cast<char>(std::tolower(static_cast<unsigned char>(s[digits])));
+        value = value << 4u | static_cast<std::uint32_t>(c <= '9' ? c - '0' : c - 'a' + 10);
+        ++digits;
+    }
+    if (digits == 0u || digits > 8u) return std::nullopt;
+    s.remove_prefix(digits);
+    return value;
+}
+
+// "_L a b", with an optional comment after it.
+std::optional<CodeLine> code_line(std::string_view rest) {
+    const auto a = hex_word(rest);
+    if (!a) return std::nullopt;
+    const auto b = hex_word(rest);
+    if (!b) return std::nullopt;
+    rest = trim(rest);
+    if (!rest.empty() && rest[0] != '#' && rest.substr(0, 2) != "//") return std::nullopt;
+    return CodeLine{*a, *b};
+}
+
+// --- Running a cheat ---------------------------------------------------------
+
+constexpr std::uint32_t kUserBase = 0x08800000u;
+
+// A code's address field: an offset from the game's memory.
+std::uint32_t address_of(std::uint32_t field) { return (kUserBase + (field & 0x0FFFFFFFu)) & 0x3FFFFFFFu; }
+
+class Pass {
+public:
+    Pass(Memory &memory, RunResult &result) : memory_(memory), result_(result) {}
+
+    [[nodiscard]] bool valid(std::uint32_t address, std::uint32_t size) const {
+        return memory_.valid(address & 0x3FFFFFFFu, size);
+    }
+
+    // Little-endian, byte by byte, so an unaligned address works as on PPSSPP.
+    [[nodiscard]] std::uint32_t read(std::uint32_t address, std::uint32_t size) const {
+        std::uint32_t value = 0u;
+        for (std::uint32_t i = 0; i < size; ++i)
+            value |= static_cast<std::uint32_t>(memory_.read8((address + i) & 0x3FFFFFFFu)) << (8u * i);
+        return value;
+    }
+
+    // Reads `size` bytes when they are valid.
+    [[nodiscard]] std::optional<std::uint32_t> try_read(std::uint32_t address, std::uint32_t size) const {
+        if (!valid(address, size)) return std::nullopt;
+        return read(address, size);
+    }
+
+    void write(std::uint32_t address, std::uint32_t value, std::uint32_t size) {
+        if (!valid(address, size)) return;
+        if (memory_.code(address & 0x3FFFFFFFu, size)) {
+            result_.wrote_code = true;
+            return;
+        }
+        for (std::uint32_t i = 0; i < size; ++i)
+            memory_.write8((address + i) & 0x3FFFFFFFu, static_cast<std::uint8_t>(value >> (8u * i)));
+    }
+
+    void copy(std::uint32_t from, std::uint32_t to, std::uint32_t length) {
+        if (length == 0u || !valid(from, length) || !valid(to, length)) return;
+        if (memory_.code(to & 0x3FFFFFFFu, length)) {
+            result_.wrote_code = true;
+            return;
+        }
+        std::vector<std::uint8_t> bytes(length);
+        for (std::uint32_t i = 0; i < length; ++i) bytes[i] = memory_.read8((from + i) & 0x3FFFFFFFu);
+        for (std::uint32_t i = 0; i < length; ++i) memory_.write8((to + i) & 0x3FFFFFFFu, bytes[i]);
+    }
+
+private:
+    Memory &memory_;
+    RunResult &result_;
+};
+
+// The comparisons: 0 equal, 1 not equal, 2 less, 3 greater, on signed values
+// as PPSSPP compares them (which matters only for 32-bit ones).
+std::optional<bool> compare(std::uint32_t condition, std::int64_t memory, std::int64_t value) {
+    switch (condition) {
+    case 0: return memory == value;
+    case 1: return memory != value;
+    case 2: return memory < value;
+    case 3: return memory > value;
+    default: return std::nullopt;
+    }
+}
+
+std::int64_t signed_value(std::uint32_t value, std::uint32_t size) {
+    return size == 4u ? static_cast<std::int64_t>(static_cast<std::int32_t>(value)) : static_cast<std::int64_t>(value);
+}
+
+std::int32_t sign_extend12(std::uint32_t value) {
+    return static_cast<std::int32_t>(value << 20u) >> 20;
+}
+
+} // namespace
+
+CheatFile parse(std::string_view text, std::string_view disc_id) {
+    CheatFile file;
+    if (text.size() >= 3u && static_cast<unsigned char>(text[0]) == 0xEFu &&
+        static_cast<unsigned char>(text[1]) == 0xBBu && static_cast<unsigned char>(text[2]) == 0xBFu) {
+        file.byte_order_mark = true;
+        text.remove_prefix(3);
+    }
+    file.crlf = text.find("\r\n") != std::string_view::npos;
+    for (std::size_t start = 0u; start <= text.size();) {
+        std::size_t end = text.find('\n', start);
+        if (end == std::string_view::npos) end = text.size();
+        std::string_view line = text.substr(start, end - start);
+        if (!line.empty() && line.back() == '\r') line.remove_suffix(1);
+        file.text.emplace_back(line);
+        start = end + 1u;
+    }
+    if (!file.text.empty() && file.text.back().empty()) file.text.pop_back();
+
+    // Each cheat with the game its section names.
+    struct Found {
+        Cheat cheat;
+        std::string section;
+    };
+    std::vector<Found> found;
+    std::size_t sections = 0u;
+    std::string section;
+    bool in_cheat = false;
+    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < file.text.size(); ++i) {
+        const std::string_view line = trim(file.text[i]);
+        if (line.empty() || line[0] == '#' || line.substr(0, 2) == "//") continue;
+        if (line[0] != '_' || line.size() < 2u) {
+            ++file.problems;
+            continue;
+        }
+        const char kind = static_cast<char>(std::toupper(static_cast<unsigned char>(line[1])));
+        const std::string_view rest = line.substr(2);
+        switch (kind) {
+        case 'S':
+            ++sections;
+            section = id_key(trim(rest));
+            in_cheat = false;
+            break;
+        case 'G': break;
+        case 'C': {
+            if (rest.empty() || !std::isdigit(static_cast<unsigned char>(rest[0]))) {
+                ++file.problems;
+                in_cheat = false;
+                break;
+            }
+            Found f;
+            f.cheat.enabled = rest[0] != '0';
+            f.cheat.name = std::string(trim(rest.substr(1)));
+            f.cheat.header_line = i;
+            f.section = section;
+            found.push_back(std::move(f));
+            in_cheat = true;
+            break;
+        }
+        case 'L':
+            if (!in_cheat) {
+                ++file.problems;
+                break;
+            }
+            if (const auto code = code_line(rest)) found.back().cheat.lines.push_back(*code);
+            else ++file.problems;
+            break;
+        case 'M':
+            if (in_cheat) found.back().cheat.action_replay = true;
+            else ++file.problems;
+            break;
+        default: ++file.problems; break;
+        }
+    }
+    const std::string game = id_key(disc_id);
+    for (Found &f : found)
+        if (sections <= 1u || f.section == game) file.cheats.push_back(std::move(f.cheat));
+    return file;
+}
+
+void set_enabled(CheatFile &file, std::size_t index, bool enabled) {
+    if (index >= file.cheats.size()) return;
+    Cheat &cheat = file.cheats[index];
+    cheat.enabled = enabled;
+    std::string &line = file.text[cheat.header_line];
+    const std::size_t at = line.find_first_not_of(" \t");
+    if (at != std::string::npos && at + 2u < line.size()) line[at + 2u] = enabled ? '1' : '0';
+}
+
+std::string text_of(const CheatFile &file) {
+    std::string out = file.byte_order_mark ? "\xEF\xBB\xBF" : "";
+    for (const std::string &line : file.text) {
+        out += line;
+        out += file.crlf ? "\r\n" : "\n";
+    }
+    return out;
+}
+
+RunResult run(const Cheat &cheat, Memory &memory, std::uint32_t buttons) {
+    RunResult result;
+    if (!cheat.enabled || cheat.action_replay) return result;
+    Pass pass(memory, result);
+    const std::vector<CodeLine> &lines = cheat.lines;
+    const std::size_t n = lines.size();
+    const auto end_invalid = [&result] { result.invalid = true; };
+    std::size_t i = 0u;
+    while (i < n) {
+        const std::uint32_t a = lines[i].a, b = lines[i].b;
+        const CodeLine *next = i + 1u < n ? &lines[i + 1u] : nullptr;
+        switch (a >> 28) {
+        case 0x0: {
+            // Written as wide as the value is.
+            const std::uint32_t size = (b & 0xFFFF0000u) != 0u ? 4u : (b & 0xFF00u) != 0u ? 2u : 1u;
+            pass.write(address_of(a), b, size);
+            i += 1u;
+            break;
+        }
+        case 0x1:
+            pass.write(address_of(a), b & 0xFFFFu, 2u);
+            i += 1u;
+            break;
+        case 0x2:
+            pass.write(address_of(a), b, 4u);
+            i += 1u;
+            break;
+        case 0x3: {
+            // Add or subtract at the address in the second word.
+            const std::uint32_t form = (a >> 20) & 0xFu;
+            const std::uint32_t target = address_of(b);
+            std::uint32_t size = 0u, amount = 0u;
+            bool add = true;
+            switch (form) {
+            case 1: case 2: size = 1u; amount = a & 0xFFu; add = form == 1u; break;
+            case 3: case 4: size = 2u; amount = a & 0xFFFFu; add = form == 3u; break;
+            case 5: case 6:
+                if (next == nullptr) return end_invalid(), result;
+                size = 4u;
+                amount = next->a;
+                add = form == 5u;
+                break;
+            default: return end_invalid(), result;
+            }
+            if (const auto value = pass.try_read(target, size))
+                pass.write(target, add ? *value + amount : *value - amount, size);
+            i += size == 4u ? 2u : 1u;
+            break;
+        }
+        case 0x4:
+        case 0x8: {
+            // A run of writes: count and step on this line, the first value and
+            // how much it grows on the next.
+            if (next == nullptr) return end_invalid(), result;
+            const std::uint32_t start = address_of(a);
+            const std::uint32_t count = b >> 16;
+            std::uint32_t size = 4u, value = next->a;
+            if (a >> 28 == 0x8u) {
+                size = (next->a >> 16) == 0u ? 1u : 2u;
+                value = size == 1u ? next->a & 0xFFu : next->a & 0xFFFFu;
+            }
+            const std::uint64_t step = static_cast<std::uint64_t>(b & 0xFFFFu) * size;
+            const std::uint64_t span = count * step + size;  // as PPSSPP measures it
+            if (count != 0u && span < 24u * 1024u * 1024u && pass.valid(start, static_cast<std::uint32_t>(span)))
+                for (std::uint32_t k = 0; k < count; ++k)
+                    pass.write(start + static_cast<std::uint32_t>(k * step), value + k * next->b, size);
+            i += 2u;
+            break;
+        }
+        case 0x5:
+            if (next == nullptr) return end_invalid(), result;
+            pass.copy(address_of(a), address_of(next->a), b);
+            i += 2u;
+            break;
+        case 0x6: {
+            // Through a pointer: the second line says how far from it, how to
+            // write, and how many more lines of steps follow.
+            if (next == nullptr) return end_invalid(), result;
+            const std::uint32_t location = address_of(a);
+            std::uint32_t value = b;
+            const std::uint32_t c = next->a;
+            const std::int32_t offset = static_cast<std::int32_t>(next->b);
+            const std::uint32_t type = (c >> 16) & 0xFu;
+            const std::uint32_t base_offset = static_cast<std::uint32_t>(sign_extend12(c >> 20) * 4);
+            const std::uint32_t listed = c & 0xFFFFu;
+            const auto first = pass.try_read(location + base_offset, 4u);
+            if (!first) {
+                // The extra lines then run as codes of their own.
+                i += 2u;
+                break;
+            }
+            std::uint32_t base = *first;
+            bool write = true;
+            const std::size_t extras = listed > 0u ? listed - 1u : 0u;
+            for (std::size_t k = 0; k < extras && i + 2u + k < n; ++k) {
+                const CodeLine &e = lines[i + 2u + k];
+                switch (e.a >> 28) {
+                case 0x1: {
+                    const auto from = pass.try_read(location, 4u);
+                    const auto to = pass.try_read(location + base_offset, 4u);
+                    if (from && to)
+                        pass.copy(*from + static_cast<std::uint32_t>(offset), *to + (e.a & 0x0FFFFFFFu), value);
+                    write = false;
+                    break;
+                }
+                case 0x2:
+                case 0x3: {
+                    const auto step = [&pass, &base](std::uint32_t field, bool subtract) {
+                        const std::uint32_t delta = field & 0x0FFFFFFFu;
+                        const std::uint32_t at = subtract ? base - delta : base + delta;
+                        const auto pointer = pass.try_read(at, 4u);
+                        if (pointer) base = *pointer;
+                        return pointer.has_value();
+                    };
+                    if (step(e.a, e.a >> 28 == 0x3u) && (e.b >> 28 == 0x2u || e.b >> 28 == 0x3u))
+                        (void)step(e.b, e.b >> 28 == 0x3u);
+                    break;
+                }
+                case 0x9:
+                    base += e.a & 0x0FFFFFFFu;
+                    value += e.b;
+                    break;
+                default: break;
+                }
+            }
+            if (write && type <= 5u) {
+                const std::uint32_t size = type % 3u == 0u ? 1u : type % 3u == 1u ? 2u : 4u;
+                const std::uint32_t at = type < 3u ? base + static_cast<std::uint32_t>(offset)
+                                                   : base - static_cast<std::uint32_t>(offset);
+                pass.write(at, value, size);
+            }
+            i += std::max<std::size_t>(2u, static_cast<std::size_t>(listed) + 1u);
+            break;
+        }
+        case 0x7: {
+            const std::uint32_t target = address_of(a);
+            const std::uint32_t op = b >> 16;
+            if (op > 5u) return end_invalid(), result;
+            const std::uint32_t size = op % 2u == 0u ? 1u : 2u;
+            const std::uint32_t operand = size == 1u ? b & 0xFFu : b & 0xFFFFu;
+            if (const auto value = pass.try_read(target, size)) {
+                const std::uint32_t v = op < 2u ? *value | operand : op < 4u ? *value & operand : *value ^ operand;
+                pass.write(target, v, size);
+            }
+            i += 1u;
+            break;
+        }
+        case 0xA:  // PPSSPP's own (rumble, shader settings): nothing to do here
+        case 0xB:  // a delay, which PPSSPP does not do either
+            i += 1u;
+            break;
+        case 0xC:
+            // The rest of the cheat runs only while memory holds the value.
+            if (const auto value = pass.try_read(address_of(a), 4u); value && *value != b) return result;
+            i += 1u;
+            break;
+        case 0xD: {
+            const std::uint32_t form = b >> 28;
+            if (form == 0u || form == 2u) {
+                // The next line runs only if the test holds.
+                const std::uint32_t size = form == 0u ? 2u : 1u;
+                const std::uint32_t value = form == 0u ? b & 0xFFFFu : b & 0xFFu;
+                const auto memory_value = pass.try_read(address_of(a), size);
+                const auto holds = compare((b >> 20) & 0xFu, memory_value.value_or(0u), value);
+                if (!holds) return end_invalid(), result;
+                i += 1u;
+                if (!memory_value || !*holds) i += 1u;
+            } else if (form == 1u || form == 3u) {
+                // Buttons: the next lines run only while they are held (1) or
+                // not all held (3).
+                const std::uint32_t mask = b & 0x0FFFFFFFu;
+                const bool held = (buttons & mask) == mask;
+                i += 1u;
+                if (form == 1u ? !held : held) i += (a & 0xFFu) + 1u;
+            } else if (form >= 4u && form <= 7u) {
+                // Two addresses compared; the next line has the size and how
+                // many lines a failed test skips.
+                if (next == nullptr) return end_invalid(), result;
+                const std::uint32_t size_code = next->b & 0xFu;
+                const std::uint32_t size = size_code < 3u ? 1u << size_code : 0u;
+                const std::uint32_t first = address_of(a), second = address_of(b);
+                std::optional<bool> holds;
+                if (size == 0u) {
+                    holds = compare(form - 4u, 0, 0);
+                } else if (const auto x = pass.try_read(first, size), y = pass.try_read(second, size); x && y) {
+                    holds = compare(form - 4u, signed_value(*x, size), signed_value(*y, size));
+                } else {
+                    holds = false;
+                }
+                i += 2u;
+                if (!*holds) i += next->a;
+            } else {
+                return end_invalid(), result;
+            }
+            break;
+        }
+        case 0xE: {
+            // The next lines run only if the test holds: 8-bit for E1, else 16-bit.
+            const bool byte = a >> 24 == 0xE1u;
+            const std::uint32_t size = byte ? 1u : 2u;
+            const std::uint32_t value = byte ? a & 0xFFu : a & 0xFFFFu;
+            const std::uint32_t skip = byte ? (a >> 16) & 0xFFu : (a >> 16) & 0xFFFu;
+            const auto memory_value = pass.try_read(address_of(b), size);
+            const auto holds = compare(b >> 28, memory_value.value_or(0u), value);
+            if (!holds) return end_invalid(), result;
+            i += 1u;
+            if (!memory_value || !*holds) i += skip;
+            break;
+        }
+        default: return end_invalid(), result;
+        }
+    }
+    return result;
+}
+
+} // namespace portablekit::cheats
diff --git a/host/cheats/cwcheat.hpp b/host/cheats/cwcheat.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2092846
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/cheats/cwcheat.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+#pragma once
+
+// CWCheat files and codes, read and run as PPSSPP reads and runs them, so a
+// player's PPSSPP cheat file gives the same results here. Only the format and
+// its meaning follow PPSSPP; the code is this project's own.
+//
+// A file (memory stick PSP/Cheats/<DISCID>.ini) is text: "_S ULUS-10566" names
+// the game, "_G" its title, "_C1 name" starts a cheat that is on ("_C0": off;
+// any digit but 0 is on), and "_L 0x20123456 0x00000063" is one line of a
+// cheat's code. "#" and "//" start comments. "_M" lines are Action Replay
+// codes, which are read but not run.
+//
+// Every cheat that is on runs from its first line each pass; a pass is every
+// 77 ms of the game's time (cheats.cpp). An address in a code is an offset from
+// 0x08800000, the start of the game's memory; pointers read from memory are
+// used as they are.
+
+#include <cstddef>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <string>
+#include <string_view>
+#include <vector>
+
+namespace portablekit::cheats {
+
+struct CodeLine {
+    std::uint32_t a{};
+    std::uint32_t b{};
+};
+
+struct Cheat {
+    std::string name;
+    bool enabled{};
+    std::size_t header_line{};  // the "_C" line's index in CheatFile::text
+    std::vector<CodeLine> lines;
+    bool action_replay{};  // it has "_M" lines: not run
+};
+
+struct CheatFile {
+    std::vector<std::string> text;  // the file's lines, without their line endings
+    std::vector<Cheat> cheats;      // for this game, in the file's order
+    std::size_t problems{};         // lines that could not be read (skipped, as PPSSPP does)
+    bool byte_order_mark{};
+    bool crlf{};
+};
+
+// Reads a file's text for the game `disc_id` ("ULUS10566"; dashes and case do
+// not matter). A file with one "_S" or none is all this game's, whatever it
+// names; with several, only the sections naming this game are.
+[[nodiscard]] CheatFile parse(std::string_view text, std::string_view disc_id);
+// Turns a cheat on or off in the file's text (its "_C" line), as PPSSPP's
+// cheat screen writes it: "_C1" or "_C0".
+void set_enabled(CheatFile &file, std::size_t index, bool enabled);
+// The file's text again, with its byte order mark and line endings.
+[[nodiscard]] std::string text_of(const CheatFile &file);
+
+// The memory cheats run against: the game's addresses, as a PSP sees them.
+class Memory {
+public:
+    virtual ~Memory() = default;
+    // The whole range is memory a cheat may read and write.
+    [[nodiscard]] virtual bool valid(std::uint32_t address, std::uint32_t size) const = 0;
+    [[nodiscard]] virtual std::uint8_t read8(std::uint32_t address) const = 0;
+    virtual void write8(std::uint32_t address, std::uint8_t value) = 0;
+    // The range holds recompiled code, which a write cannot change here: the
+    // write is left out and the cheat counts as changing code.
+    [[nodiscard]] virtual bool code(std::uint32_t address, std::uint32_t size) const = 0;
+};
+
+struct RunResult {
+    bool wrote_code{};  // a write into code was left out
+    bool invalid{};     // a line it cannot run ended this pass early
+};
+
+// One pass of a cheat. `buttons` are the PSP's pad buttons held now
+// (sceCtrl's bits), for the codes that test them.
+RunResult run(const Cheat &cheat, Memory &memory, std::uint32_t buttons);
+
+} // namespace portablekit::cheats
